\[
\mathcal{S}_k \xrightarrow{\ C_k\ } \mathcal{S}'_k \xrightarrow{\ R_k\ } \mathcal{S}_{k+1}.
\]


\end{definition}

Examples include thermodynamic dissipation vs.\ energy input, mutation vs.\ DNA repair, synaptic pruning vs.\ synaptic strengthening, decoherence vs.\ recoherence, and noise vs.\ error correction.

\subsection{Universal Resilience Law}

\begin{theorem}[Universal Resilience Law]
A system persists, stabilizes, or grows if and only if


\[
\prod_{k=1}^{\infty} \frac{R_k}{C_k} \ge 1.
